  1. Extract the Urban Crash data from the Socrata API
   → use your working extractor script (10-20k records)
   → upload raw data to bronze container

2. Build AzureBlobHandler class (OOP pattern)
   → mirrors your S3Handler concept
   → methods: upload_dataframe, download_dataframe, list_files
   → import this into all Azure pipeline scripts

3. Schema validation with Pandera
   → inspect the raw API fields first (run a 5-row sample)
   → build Pandera schema for the crash dataset
   → run PII audit (lat/lon, location fields need checking)

4. Build silver layer transform
   → clean categoricals (Snow vs SNOW issue from your project notes)
   → standardize column names
   → drop irrelevant columns (vehicle ID, report number, metadata)
   → validate schema at bronze → silver transition

5. Build gold layer
   → crash hotspots by location bucket
   → severity distribution over time
   → weather + surface condition correlations
   → DUI / substance abuse frequency by area

6. Wire it all into a Prefect flow
   → extract → validate → transform → upload bronze → silver → gold